        "title": "Gödel's Incompleteness Theorems",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The two incompleteness theorems (1931) are the most profound results in the foundations of\nmathematics. They place absolute limits on what formal systems can prove about themselves.\nEvery sufficiently strong consistent formal system is incomplete — and cannot prove its own\nconsistency."
